# BMAD + Beads Agent Instructions

> **Context Recovery**: Run `bd prime` after compaction, clear, or new session
> Hooks auto-call this in Claude Code when .beads/ detected

---

## The Split: Who Owns What

```
BMAD (Formal Outputs):              Beads (Runtime & Coordination):
├── Documents                       ├── Work claims (bd-claim)
├── sprint-status.yaml              ├── Runtime decisions (bd-decision)
├── workflow-status.yaml            ├── Blockers (bd-blocker)
├── ADRs (architecture.md)          ├── HALTs (bd-halt)
├── Task checkboxes (story files)   ├── Cross-story dependencies
└── Code review findings            └── Action items (bd-action)
```

**Rule**: Don't duplicate. BMAD handles formal outputs. Beads handles runtime state.

---

## Session Start

```bash
bd-status              # Ready work + blockers (one command)
bd-claim "story-key"   # Claim before starting work
```

## During Work

```bash
bd-decision "title"    # Runtime decision (outside workflow)
bd-blocker "title"     # External blocker
bd-halt "reason"       # Critical failure (priority 0)
bd-action "title"      # Action item
```

## Session End

```bash
bd-release <id>        # Release claim (if you claimed)
git add <files>        # Stage changes
git commit -m "..."    # Hooks auto-sync Beads
git push               # Push to remote
```

> **Note**: Git hooks auto-sync Beads on commit. Manual `bd sync` only needed if hooks aren't installed.

---

## Priority Scale (Numbers Only)

| Priority | Use For | Quick Create |
|----------|---------|--------------|
| 0 | HALT, critical failures | `bd-halt "reason"` |
| 1 | Work claims, urgent blockers | `bd-blocker "title"` |
| 2 | Decisions, action items | `bd-decision "title"` |
| 3-4 | Low/backlog | manual `bd create` |

---

## Quick Reference

| Command | What It Does |
|---------|--------------|
| `bd-status` | Ready work + blockers |
| `bd-next` | Ready work only |
| `bd-claim X` | Claim story before starting |
| `bd-release X` | Release claim |
| `bd-halt X` | Create HALT (priority 0) |
| `bd-decision X` | Create runtime decision |
| `bd-blocker X` | Create blocker |
| `bd-action X` | Create action item |
| `bd-who` | See who's working on what |
| `bd-help` | Show all commands |

---

## What NOT to Track in Beads

These belong in BMAD files:
- Story status → `sprint-status.yaml`
- Phase progress → `workflow-status.yaml`
- ADRs → `architecture.md`
- Task checkboxes → story files
- Code review findings → story files

---

## What TO Track in Beads

- **Work claims** - Prevent concurrent edits
- **Runtime decisions** - Choices made OUTSIDE formal workflows
- **External blockers** - Waiting on APIs, approvals, etc.
- **HALTs** - Critical failures that must persist
- **Cross-story deps** - Story B needs Story A
- **Action items** - Cross-epic visibility

---

